                                                                  <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/6feb0129cdbeb92c> ;
                                              gutprop:locatedIn <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12444> ;
                                              rdfs:comment "A protein complex that plays a role in both NMDA binding and ion transport. It is a heterotetramer consisting of 2 glutamate [NMDA] receptor subunit zeta-1 proteins and 2 epsilon subunits (glutamate [NMDA] receptor subunit epsilon-1, -2, -3 or -4). [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                           "NCIT Match" ;
                                              rdfs:label "N-Methyl-D-Aspartate Receptor" .


