                                                          "NCIT Match" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Cecum" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12382
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12382> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/AnatomicalSite> ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/AnatomicSite> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/e882e5c8cdc59ab7> ,
                                                                 <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/70bdae49483e37d0> ;
                                             gutprop:locatedIn <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C45247> ,
                                                               <https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0009932> ,
                                                               <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/human/PediatricChronicIntestinalPseudoObstructionPatients> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                          "The part of the large intestine measured from the cecum to the rectum consisting of ascending, transverse, descending and sigmoid portions. The purpose of the colon is to remove water from digested food prior to excretion. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Colon" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12386
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12386> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/AnatomicalSite> ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/AnatomicSite> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/1241dd498a6e2964> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                          "The section of the intestines between the pylorus and cecum. The small intestine is approximately 20 feet long and consists of the duodenum, the jejunum, and the ileum. Its main function is to absorb nutrients from food as the food is transported to the large intestine. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Small Intestine" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12387
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12387> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
