###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12468
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12468> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/AnatomicalSite> ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/AnatomicSite> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/69d651fbde41b2f0> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                          "One of a pair of viscera occupying the pulmonary cavities of the thorax, the organs of respiration in which aeration of the blood takes place. As a rule, the right lung is slightly larger than the left and is divided into three lobes (an upper, a middle, and a lower or basal), while the left has two lobes (an upper and a lower or basal). Each lung is irregularly conical in shape, presenting a blunt upper extremity (the apex), a concave base following the curve of the diaphragm, an outer convex surface (costal surface), an inner or mediastinal surface (mediastinal surface), a thin and sharp anterior border, and a thick and rounded posterior border. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Lung" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12470
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12470> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/AnatomicalSite> ;
