                                             gutprop:locatedIn <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C12439> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "Any of the conducting cells of the nervous system. A typical neuron consists of a cell body, containing the nucleus and the surrounding cytoplasm (perikaryon); several short radiating processes (dendrites); and one long process (the axon), which terminates in twiglike branches (telodendrons) and may have branches (collaterals) projecting along its course. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                          "NCIT Match" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Neuron" .


