                                            rdfs:comment "Having a high amount of body fat (body mass index [BMI] of 30 or more). [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                         "NCIT Match" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Obesity" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3298
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3298> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                     skos:Concept ,
                                                     <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/d2937a38f57d6c50> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "A condition of reduced bone mass, with decreased cortical thickness and a decrease in the number and size of the trabeculae of cancellous bone (but normal chemical composition), resulting in increased fracture incidence. Osteoporosis is classified as primary (Type 1, postmenopausal osteoporosis; Type 2, age-associated osteoporosis; and idiopathic, which can affect juveniles, premenopausal women, and middle-aged men) and secondary osteoporosis (which results from an identifiable cause of bone mass loss). [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                         "NCIT Match" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Osteoporosis" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3303
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3303> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                     skos:Concept ,
                                                     <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/5c78c8e7160e76ba> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                         "The sensation of discomfort, distress, or agony, resulting from the stimulation of specialized nerve endings. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Pain" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3318
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3318> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                     skos:Concept ,
                                                     <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/219107ace8ee7874> ;
                                            gutprop:isA <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004298> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "A mucosal erosion that occurs in the esophagus, stomach or duodenum. Symptoms can include abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting, and bleeding. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                         "NCIT Match" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Peptic Ulcer" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3340
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3340> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                     skos:Concept ,
                                                     <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/3d46464335ad914c> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "A usually exophytic mass attached to the underlying tissue by a broad base or a thin stalk.  Polyps can be neoplastic or non-neoplastic.  Neoplastic polyps usually represent proliferations of the epithelium, and are commonly seen in the gastrointestinal tract.  Polyps of the gastrointestinal tract are often called adenomas, are associated with dysplasia, and may eventually transform into carcinomas.  Non-neoplastic polyps may be inflammatory, degenerative, or the result of malformations. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                         "NCIT Match" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Polyp" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3346
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3346> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                     skos:Concept ,
                                                     <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/95b6cf097c3d557a> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "An autoimmune condition characterized by red, well-delineated plaques with silvery scales that are usually on the extensor surfaces and scalp. They can occasionally present with these manifestations: pustules; erythema and scaling in intertriginous areas, and erythroderma, that are often distributed on extensor surfaces and scalp. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                         "NCIT Match" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Psoriasis" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3362
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C3362> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                     skos:Concept ,
                                                     <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                            gutprop:affect <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OGMS_0000045> ,
                                                           <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMIT_0016272> ,
                                                           <https://disease-ontology.org/?id=DOID:10608> ;
                                            gutprop:changeAbundance <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_128827> ,
                                                                    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1678> ,
                                                                    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_174708> ,
                                                                    <https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C2584567> ,
                                                                    <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D045857> ,
                                                                    <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D052557> ;
                                            gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/a6804380352b475f> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/ae8d715b8fdebc05> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/1f204fb75593c295> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/26ff53e3b8ce5ded> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/4d4c060343baed4b> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/482e6bc134fab7a5> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/8651347d5d501956> ,
                                                                <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/883fc6ece7b0a4b1> ;
                                            gutprop:isA <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C2893> ,
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMIT_0002893> ,
                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OMIT_0005457> ,
                                                        <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/diseasedisorderorfinding/NeuropsychiatricDisorders> ;
                                            gutprop:target <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C45247> ,
                                                           <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/human/PatientsWithSchizophrenia> ,
                                                           <https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/68010361> ;
                                            rdfs:comment "A major psychotic disorder characterized by abnormalities in the perception or expression of reality. It affects the cognitive and psychomotor functions. Common clinical signs and symptoms include delusions, hallucinations, disorganized thinking, and retreat from reality. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                         "NCIT Match" ;
                                            rdfs:label "Schizophrenia" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C33715
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C33715> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/AnatomicalSite> ;
