                                                                 <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/9496e0d174d2960e> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                          "Neurodegenerative disorders are a group of conditions characterized by the progressive loss of structure or function of neurons, leading to cognitive, motor, or sensory impairment. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Neurodegenerative Disorder" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C401
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C401> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                    skos:Concept ,
                                                    gutprop:DietarySupplement ;
                                           skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DietarySupplement> ;
                                           gutprop:changeExpression <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C125468> ,
                                                                    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C21521> ;
                                           gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/c9ede648254c86cb> ;
                                           rdfs:comment "A phytopolylphenol pigment isolated from the plant Curcuma longa, commonly known as turmeric, with a variety of pharmacologic properties.  Curcumin blocks the formation of reactive-oxygen species, possesses anti-inflammatory properties as a result of inhibition of cyclooxygenases (COX) and other enzymes involved in inflammation; and disrupts cell signal transduction by various mechanisms including inhibition of protein kinase C.  These effects may play a role in the agent's observed antineoplastic properties, which include inhibition of tumor cell proliferation and suppression of chemically induced carcinogenesis and tumor growth in animal models of cancer. (NCI04) [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                        "NCIT Match" ;
                                           rdfs:label "Curcumin" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C40185
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C40185> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/AnatomicalSite> ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/AnatomicSite> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/556a7ccd188f0c32> ;
                                             gutprop:locatedIn <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C45247> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                          "The largest part of the brain composed of the cerebral hemispheres, thalamus, hypothalamus, and the limbic system. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Forebrain" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C40625
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C40625> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      gutprop:Chemical ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Chemical> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/949e357dba8ab74a> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "Biogenic Amine Metabolism involves anabolic and catabolic biochemical changes to a type of nitrogen containing hydrocarbons (biogenic amines) involved in signaling as neurotransmitters or hormones or as components of vitamins, phospholipids, or ribosomes within a cell as materials needed for important life processes. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                          "NCIT Match" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Biogenic Amine Metabolic Process" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C413
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C413> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                    skos:Concept ,
                                                    gutprop:Food ;
                                           skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Food> ;
                                           gutprop:administered <https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C0679646> ;
                                           gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/a4645eb49a2e2fcd> ,
                                                               <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/5f9d0f663c0cec62> ;
                                           gutprop:impact <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_1578> ;
                                           rdfs:comment "Food made from the milk of some mammals, most commonly cows, goats and sheep. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                        "NCIT Match" ;
                                           rdfs:label "Dairy Product" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C41366
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C41366> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/DiseaseDisorderOrFinding> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/053bca52bc530700> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "A genetic predisposition to form IgE antibodies in response to exposure to allergens and therefore, for the development of immediate (type I) hypersensitivity and atopic conditions, such as allergic rhinitis; bronchial asthma, atopic dermatitis, and food allergy. Mutations of specific alleles on the long arm of chromosome 5 have been associated with higher levels of IL-4 and IgE and are known as IL-4 promoter polymorphisms. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ,
                                                          "NCIT Match" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Atopy" .


###  http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C43572
<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C43572> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                      skos:Concept ,
                                                      <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/Gene> ;
                                             skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Gene> ;
                                             gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/6451f0e76b77341f> ;
                                             rdfs:comment "NCIT Match" ,
                                                          "Parafibromin (531 aa, ~61 kDa) is encoded by the human CDC73 gene. This protein plays a role in the regulation of both gene transcription and histone ubiquitination. [Definition Source: NCIT]" ;
                                             rdfs:label "Parafibromin" .


