###  https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C1097411
<https://uts.nlm.nih.gov/uts/umls/concept/C1097411> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                             skos:Concept ,
                                                             <https://w3id.org/brainteaser/ontology/schema/Gene> ;
                                                    skos:inScheme <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/schema/conceptScheme/Gene> ;
                                                    gutprop:containedIn <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/mention/8d5200e45064766f> ;
                                                    rdfs:comment "A mammalian enzyme composed of a heterodimer of alpha and beta subunits. Each subunit consists of four domains; N-terminal HNOX domain, PAS-like domain, a coiled-coil domain, and a C-terminal catalytic domain. All four domains are homologous proteins with a similar conformation of functional domains. Soluble guanylate cyclase catalyzes the formation of cyclic GMP from GTP, and is a key enzyme of the nitric oxide signaling pathway involved in the regulation of a variety of biological and physiological processes in mammals. [Definition Source: UMLS]" ,
                                                                 "UMLS Match" ;
                                                    rdfs:label "Soluble Guanylyl Cyclase" .


