                                                                                           dcterms:creator "Samuel Piron" ;
                                                                                           rdfs:comment "The \"dormant blood microbiome\" refers to a hypothetical or theoretical community of microorganisms that are present in the blood but are not actively metabolizing or replicating, potentially remaining in a dormant or quiescent state. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
