<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36738999_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36738999> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Similar to CRS model, short-term HCD intervention induced anxiety and depression-like behavior behavioral abnormalities in mice." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36738999_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Targeting the gut-microbiota-brain axis in irritable bowel disease to improve cognitive function - recent knowledge and emerging therapeutic opportunities." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The brain-gut axis forms a bidirectional communication system between the gastrointestinal (GI) tract and cognitive brain areas." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "This adds to the growing body of evidence supporting targeted therapeutic strategies to modulate the gut microbiota for the treatment of brain/mental-health-related disease." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Disturbances to this system in disease states such as inflammatory bowel disease have consequences for neuronal activity and subsequent cognitive function." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut-microbiota-brain axis refers to the communication between gut-resident bacteria and the brain." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This circuits exists to detect gut microorganisms and relay information to specific areas of the central nervous system (CNS) that in turn, regulate gut physiology." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Changes in both the stability and diversity of the gut microbiota have been implicated in several neuronal disorders, including depression, autism spectrum disorder Parkinson's disease, Alzheimer's disease and multiple sclerosis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Correcting this imbalance with medicinal herbs, the metabolic products of dysregulated bacteria and probiotics have shown hope for the treatment of these neuronal disorders." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this review, we focus on recent advances in our understanding of the intricate connections between the gut-microbiota and the brain." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We discuss the contribution of gut microbiota to neuronal disorders and the tangible links between diseases of the GI tract with cognitive function and behaviour." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36757367_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36757367> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this regard, we focus on irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) given its strong links to brain function and anxiety disorders." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36757367_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alteration of faecal microbiota balance related to long-term deep meditation." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Advancements in research have confirmed that gut microbiota can influence health through the microbiota-gut-brain axis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The α-diversity indices of the meditation and control groups differed significantly." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the genus level, <i>Prevotella</i> and <i>Bacteroides</i> were significantly enriched in the meditation group." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "According to the LEfSe analysis, two beneficial bacterial genera (<i>Megamonas</i> and <i>Faecalibacterium</i>) were significantly enriched in the meditation group." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Functional predictive analysis further showed that several pathways-including glycan biosynthesis, metabolism and lipopolysaccharide biosynthesis-were significantly enriched in the meditation group." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_14
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_14> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Moreover, plasma levels of clinical risk factors were significantly decreased in the meditation group, including total cholesterol and apolipoprotein B." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_14" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_15
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_15> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Long-term traditional Tibetan Buddhist meditation may positively impact physical and mental health." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_15" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_16
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_16> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "We confirmed that the gut microbiota composition differed between the monks and control subjects." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_16" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_17
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_17> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The microbiota enriched in monks was associated with a reduced risk of anxiety, depression and cardiovascular disease and could enhance immune function." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_17" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_18
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_18> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Overall, these results suggest that meditation plays a positive role in psychosomatic conditions and well-being." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_18" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Meditation, as an inner mental exercise, can positively impact the regulation of an individual's physical and mental health." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, few studies have comprehensively investigated faecal microbiota following long-term (several years) deep meditation." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, we propose that long-term meditation may regulate gut microbiota homeostasis and, in turn, affect physical and mental health." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "To investigate the effects of long-term deep meditation on the gut microbiome structure." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "To examine the intestinal flora, 16S rRNA gene sequencing was performed on faecal samples of 56 Tibetan Buddhist monks and neighbouring residents." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Based on the sequencing data, linear discriminant analysis effect size (LEfSe) was employed to identify differential intestinal microbial communities between the two groups." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Phylogenetic Investigation of Communities by Reconstruction of Unobserved States (PICRUSt) analysis was used to predict the function of faecal microbiota." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36760344_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36760344> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition, we evaluated biochemical indices in the plasma." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36760344_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36794003> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "High-fiber diet ameliorates gut microbiota, serum metabolism and emotional mood in type 2 diabetes patients." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Previous studies have demonstrated that patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) often had the problems of fecal microbiota dysbiosis, and were usually accompanied with psychiatric comorbidities (such as depression and anxiety)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Here, we conducted a randomized clinical study to analyze the changes in gut microbiota, serum metabolism and emotional mood of patients with T2DM after consumption of a high-fiber diet." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The glucose homeostasis of participants with T2DM was improved by the high-fiber diet, and the serum metabolome, systemic inflammation and psychiatric comorbidities were also altered." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The increased abundances of <i>Lactobacillus</i>, <i>Bifidobacterium</i> and <i>Akkermansias</i> revealed that the proportions of beneficial gut microbes were enriched by the high-fiber diet, while the abundances of <i>Desulfovibrio</i>, <i>Klebsiella</i> and other opportunistic pathogens were decreased." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36794003_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36794003> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, the current study demonstrated that the intestinal microbiota alterations which were influenced by the high-fiber diet could improve the serum metabolism and emotional mood of patients with T2DM." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36794003_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Beneficial effects of arketamine on the reduced bone mineral density in susceptible mice after chronic social defeat stress: Role of the gut-microbiota-bone-brain axis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Patients with depression exhibit reduced bone mineral density (BMD)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "This article is part of the Special Issue on \"Ketamine and its Metabolites\"." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We previously reported that the new antidepressant arketamine improved the reduced BMD seen in chronic social defeat stress (CSDS) susceptible mice and ovariectomized mice." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Considering the role of the gut microbiota in maintaining bone health, the current study investigated whether the gut microbiota, along with metabolites derived from the microbiome, play a role in the beneficial actions of arketamine with respect to the anhedonia-like behavior and reduced BMD seen in CSDS susceptible mice." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A single administration of arketamine (10 mg/kg) ameliorated anhedonia-like behavior and decreased femoral neck cortical (and total) BMD in CSDS susceptible mice." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "There was a negative correlation between anhedonia-like behavior and BMD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, significant differences in the abundance of microbiota (and plasma metabolites) were found between the CSDS + saline and CSDS + arketamine groups." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Correlations were observed between the abundance of certain microbiota (and plasma metabolites) and cortical (and total) BMD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "These data suggest that, in addition to its anti-anhedonia effect, arketamine might ameliorate the reduced cortical (and total) BMD seen in CSDS susceptible mice through the gut-microbiota-bone-brain axis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36804535_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36804535> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, arketamine could serve as a drug therapy for depressed patients with low BMD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36804535_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The Role of Gut Microbiota in Various Neurological and Psychiatric Disorders-An Evidence Mapping Based on Quantified Evidence." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We searched PubMed, Cochrane Library, and Epistemonikos to identify systematic reviews and meta-analysis (SRs)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the phylum level, <i>Firmicutes</i>, <i>Bacteroidetes</i>, <i>Actinobacteria</i>, <i>Proteobacteria</i>, and <i>Verrucomicrobia</i> were more researched." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "At the genus level, <i>Prevotella</i>, <i>Coprococcus</i>, <i>Parabacteroides</i>, <i>Phascolarctobacterium</i>, <i>Escherichia Shigella</i>, <i>Alistipes</i>, <i>Sutteralla</i>, <i>Veillonella</i>, <i>Odoribacter</i>, <i>Faecalibacterium</i>, <i>Bacteroides</i>, <i>Bifidobacterium</i>, <i>Dialister</i>, and <i>Blautia</i> were more researched." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Some diseases have been found to have specific flora changes, and some diseases have been found to have common intestinal microbiological changes." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found varied levels of evidence for the associations between gut microbiota and neurological diseases; some gut microbiota increased the risk of neurological diseases, whereas others showed evidence of benefit that gut microbiota might be promising therapeutic targets for such diseases." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We searched for neurological diseases and psychiatric disorders, including Alzheimer's disease (AD), attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD), amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), autism spectrum disorder (ASD), anorexia nervosa (AN), bipolar disorder (BD), eating disorder (ED), generalized anxiety disorder (GAD), major depressive disorder (MDD), multiple sclerosis (MS), obsessive compulsive disorder (OCD), Parkinson's disease (PD), posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD), spinal cord injury (SCI), schizophrenia, and stroke." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We used A Measurement Tool to Assess Systematic Reviews (AMSTAR-2) to evaluate the quality of included SRs." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We also created an evidence map showing the role of gut microbiota in neurological diseases and the certainty of the evidence." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In total, 42 studies were included in this evidence mapping." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most findings were obtained from observational studies." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "According to the AMSTAR-2 assessment, 21 SRs scored \"critically low\" in terms of methodological quality, 16 SR scored \"low,\" and 5 SR scored \"moderate.\"" ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A total of 15 diseases have been investigated for the potential association between gut microbiome alpha diversity and disease, with the Shannon index and Simpson index being the most widely studied." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36816743_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36816743> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A total of 12 diseases were investigated for potential link between beta diversity and disease." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36816743_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Brain, Gut, and Immune Interconnections in Psychiatric Disorders: Implications for Treatment." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent studies have linked the gut microbiota to psychiatric symptoms and disorders through complex bidirectional networks." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The purpose of the current article is to describe the associations between the gut microbiota and brain in psychiatric disorders." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Although there are no approved treatments, there are global efforts underway to find more accurate measures to guide treatment and research." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this brief review, we describe current conceptualizations regarding the complex interconnections between psychiatric disorders and the gut microbiota." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "[<i>Journal of Psychosocial Nursing and Mental Health Services, 61</i>(3), 7-11." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36881806_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36881806> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "]." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36881806_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fermented Wheat Germ Alleviates Depression-like Behavior in Rats with Chronic and Unpredictable Mild Stress." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Depression is a chronic mental illness with devastating effects on a person's physical and mental health." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The results demonstrated that FWG improved depression-like behaviors and increased neurotransmitter levels in the hippocampus of CUMS model rats." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition, FWG effectively altered the gut microbiota structure and remodeled the gut microbiota in CUMS rats, restored neurotransmitter levels in depressed rats through the brain-gut axis, and restored amino acid metabolic functions." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "In conclusion, we suggest that FWG has antidepressant effects, and its potential mechanism may act by restoring the disordered brain-gut axis." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies have reported that food fermentation with probiotics can enrich the nutritional values of food and produce functional microorganisms that can alleviate depression and anxiety." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Wheat germ is an inexpensive raw material that is rich in bioactive ingredients." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "For example, gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) is reported to have antidepressant effects." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Several studies concluded that <i>Lactobacillus plantarum</i> is a GABA-producing bacteria and can alleviate depression." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Herein, fermented wheat germs (FWGs) were used to treat stress-induced depression." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "FWG was prepared by fermenting wheat germs with <i>Lactobacillus plantarum</i>." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The chronic unpredictable mild stress (CUMS) model was established in rats, and these rats were treated with FWG for four weeks to evaluate the effects of FWG in relieving depression." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36900437_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36900437> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition, the study also analyzed the potential anti-depressive mechanism of FWG based on behavioral changes, physiological and biochemical index changes, and intestinal flora changes in depressed rats." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36900437_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Effect of date seed (<i>Phoenix dactylifera</i>) supplementation as functional food on cardiometabolic risk factors, metabolic endotoxaemia and mental health in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus: a blinded randomised controlled trial protocol." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recently, the improvement of chronic hyperglycaemia-related damage of type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) through functional food consumption has attracted the attention of many clinicians." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The study protocol was approved by the Ethical Committee of the Tabriz University of Medical Sciences, Tabriz, Iran (code: IR.TBZMED.REC.1400.752)." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Iranian Registry of Clinical Trials (www.irct.ir/IRCT20150205020965N10)." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study aims to determine the effectiveness of date seed powder (DSP) as a functional food (prebiotic) on the cardiometabolic risk factors, oxidative stress, anti-/inflammatory biomarkers, metabolic endotoxaemia (gut microbiota), adipokines, hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis biomarkers, immune system, anthropometric indices and mental health in patients with T2DM." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study protocol will be conducted as randomised, triple-blind, placebo-controlled trial with the inclusion of 48 patients with T2DM." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The participants will be randomly assigned into two equal groups of intervention (n=24) and placebo (n=24) and receive 5 g/day of DSP or placebo for 8 weeks, respectively." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "At baseline and post-intervention, fasting blood samples will be collected to assess the serum levels of lipid profile, glycaemic indices, antioxidant and oxidative stress, anti-/inflammatory biomarkers, lipopolysaccharide, 8-hydroxy-guanine, adipokines, hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis biomarkers, immune system and mental health." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Data will be analysed using the SPSS software (V.16.0)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "To compare the quantitative variables, paired and unpaired Student's t-tests and covariance analyses will be used." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In this study, the potential effects of DSP on patients with T2DM will be evaluated for the first time." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36931666_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36931666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is hoped that the results would increase the body of scientific knowledge about DSP supplementation on the cardiometabolic risk factors, oxidative stress, anti-/inflammatory biomarkers, metabolic endotoxaemia, adipokines, hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis biomarkers, immune system, anthropometric indices and mental health in patients with T2DM." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36931666_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Evaluating the effectiveness of probiotics in relieving constipation in Parkinson's disease: A systematic review and meta-analysis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The aim of this study was to evaluate the effects of probiotics on the treatment of constipation in patients with Parkinson's disease (PD) by analyzing data from published randomized clinical trials (RCTs)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "We calculated a standardized mean difference (SMD) of 0.92 (95% CI, 0.65 to 1.19; I-squared = 57.0%; p < 0.001) to determine the treatment effect in terms of frequency of bowel movements per week in the RCTs." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our results show that probiotic intake has beneficial effects on constipation in PD patients." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Further research, including multicenter studies, is needed to assess the long-term efficacy and safety of probiotic supplements in neurodegenerative diseases." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "PD is a neurodegenerative disease characterized by clinical symptoms such as rigidity, bradykinesia, and resting tremor." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Constipation is a common complaint reported by PD patients." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Probiotics are often used to treat functional constipation." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The potential mechanisms behind PD-related constipation include dysfunction of the enteric nervous system due to alpha-synuclein aggregation, dyssynergic contractions of the puborectalis muscle, and alterations of the gut microbiome." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "To conduct this study, we searched Scopus, PubMed, and Google Scholar for published articles on PD, probiotics, and constipation." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We selected RCTs from 944 studies, and ultimately included 3 RCTs in our meta-analysis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The frequency of bowel movements per week was the only index that could be summarized among the records." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36938477_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36938477> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We extracted and analyzed the results as means and standard deviations." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36938477_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The Potential of Flavonoids and Flavonoid Metabolites in the Treatment of Neurodegenerative Pathology in Disorders of Cognitive Decline." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Flavonoids are a biodiverse family of dietary compounds that have antioxidant, anti-inflammatory, antiviral, and antibacterial cell protective profiles." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Native flavonoids have many beneficial properties in the alleviation of inflammation in tissues, however, concerns have been raised that therapeutic levels of flavonoids may not be achieved, thus allowing them to display optimal therapeutic effects." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dietary manipulation and vagal stimulation have both yielded beneficial responses in the treatment of autism spectrum disorders, depression, and anxiety, establishing the vagal nerve as a route of communication in the gut-brain axis with established roles in disease intervention." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "While a number of native flavonoids are beneficial in the treatment of neurological disorders and are known to penetrate the blood-brain barrier, microbiome-generated flavonoid metabolites (e.g., protocatechuic acid, urolithins, γ-valerolactones), which retain the antioxidant and anti-inflammatory potency of the native flavonoid in addition to bioactive properties that promote mitochondrial health and cerebrovascular microcapillary function, should also be considered as potential biotherapeutic agents." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies are warranted to experimentally examine the efficacy of flavonoid metabolites directly, as they emerge as novel therapeutic options." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "They have received considerable attention as potential therapeutic agents in biomedicine and have been widely used in traditional complimentary medicine for generations." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Such complimentary medical herbal formulations are extremely complex mixtures of many pharmacologically active compounds that provide a therapeutic outcome through a network pharmacological effects of considerable complexity." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Methods are emerging to determine the active components used in complimentary medicine and their therapeutic targets and to decipher the complexities of how network pharmacology provides such therapeutic effects." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiome has important roles to play in the generation of bioactive flavonoid metabolites retaining or exceeding the antioxidative and anti-inflammatory properties of the intact flavonoid and, in some cases, new antitumor and antineurodegenerative bioactivities." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Certain food items have been identified with high prebiotic profiles suggesting that neutraceutical supplementation may be beneficially employed to preserve a healthy population of bacterial symbiont species and minimize the establishment of harmful pathogenic organisms." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut health is an important consideration effecting the overall health and wellbeing of linked organ systems." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bioconversion of dietary flavonoid components in the gut generates therapeutic metabolites that can also be transported by the vagus nerve and systemic circulation to brain cell populations to exert a beneficial effect." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36978911_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36978911> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This is particularly important in a number of neurological disorders (autism, bipolar disorder, AD, PD) characterized by effects on moods, resulting in depression and anxiety, impaired motor function, and long-term cognitive decline." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36978911_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Controlling the Impact of <i>Helicobacter pylori</i>-Related Hyperhomocysteinemia on Neurodegeneration." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Helicobacter pylori</i> infection consists a high global burden affecting more than 50% of the world's population." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is implicated, beyond substantiated local gastric pathologies, i.e., peptic ulcers and gastric cancer, in the pathophysiology of several neurodegenerative disorders, mainly by inducing hyperhomocysteinemia-related brain cortical thinning (BCT)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "BCT has been advocated as a possible biomarker associated with neurodegenerative central nervous system disorders such as Alzheimer's disease, Parkinson's disease, multiple sclerosis, and/or glaucoma, termed as \"ocular Alzheimer's disease\"." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "According to the infection hypothesis in relation to neurodegeneration, <i>Helicobacter pylori</i> as non-commensal gut microbiome has been advocated as trigger and/or mediator of neurodegenerative diseases, such as the development of Alzheimer's disease." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Among others, <i>Helicobacter pylori</i>-related inflammatory mediators, defensins, autophagy, vitamin D, dietary factors, role of probiotics, and some pathogenetic considerations including relevant involved genes are discussed within this opinion article." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36984505_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36984505> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In conclusion, by controlling the impact of <i>Helicobacter pylori</i>-related hyperhomocysteinemia on neurodegenerative disorders might offer benefits, and additional research is warranted to clarify this crucial topic currently representing a major worldwide burden." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36984505_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The Role of Diet as a Modulator of the Inflammatory Process in the Neurological Diseases." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Neurological diseases are recognized as major causes of disability and mortality worldwide." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Due to the dynamic progress of diseases such as Alzheimer's disease (AD), Parkinson's Disease (PD), Schizophrenia, Depression, and Multiple Sclerosis (MD), scientists are mobilized to look for new and more effective methods of interventions." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A growing body of evidence suggests that inflammatory processes and an imbalance in the composition and function of the gut microbiome, which play a critical role in the pathogenesis of various neurological diseases and dietary interventions, such as the Mediterranean diet the DASH diet, or the ketogenic diet can have beneficial effects on their course." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The aim of this review was to take a closer look at the role of diet and its ingredients in modulating inflammation associated with the development and/or progression of central nervous system diseases." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Presented data shows that consuming a diet abundant in fruits, vegetables, nuts, herbs, spices, and legumes that are sources of anti-inflammatory elements such as omega-3 fatty acids, polyphenols, vitamins, essential minerals, and probiotics while avoiding foods that promote inflammation, create a positive brain environment and is associated with a reduced risk of neurological diseases." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36986165_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36986165> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Personalized nutritional interventions may constitute a non-invasive and effective strategy in combating neurological disorders." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36986165_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Treatment response to supplemental nutrients for ADHD is independent of diet quality: the MADDY Study RCT." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The 8-week Micronutrients for ADHD in Youth (MADDY) randomized controlled trial (<i>N</i> = 126, age 6-12) of broad-spectrum multinutrients for ADHD with emotional dysregulation found 3 times as many responders with multinutrients (54%) compared to placebo (18%) by Clinical Global Impression-Improvement (CGI-I)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our primary aim for this analysis tests the hypothesis that those with poor overall diet quality at baseline benefit more." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The second aim is to explore whether specific components of diet quality moderate treatment response." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "124 children (69 multinutrients, 55 placebo) had diet quality assessed using the Healthy Eating Index-2015 (HEI-2015)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "For each potential moderator, the outcome CGI-I at week 8 (RCT-end), was modeled two ways: (1) as a dichotomous variable: responder/non-responder, with responders defined by a rating of 1 or 2 'very much' or 'much improved,' all else equals non-responder using logistic regression, and (2) as a dimensional improvement outcome from 1 = very much improved to 7 = very much worse, using linear regression." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "HEI-2015 total score did not moderate treatment response [odds ratio = 1.00 (95% CI: 0.90,1.10), <i>p</i> = 0.984] or improvement [β = -0.01 (95% CI: -0.06,0.04), <i>p</i> = 0.648]." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, total vegetable intake moderated level of improvement in exploratory analysis [β = -0.48 (95% CI: -0.82, -0.13), <i>p</i> = 0.007]: those with higher baseline vegetable intake showed greater benefit from multinutrients compared to placebo." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multinutrients may benefit children with ADHD and irritability regardless of overall diet quality." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/36989335_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/36989335> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The finding that higher baseline vegetable intake may improve response to multinutrients deserves further exploration, including dietary effect on gut microbiota and absorption of multinutrients and parental factors." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_36989335_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Different roles of microbiota and genetics in the prediction of treatment response in major depressive disorder." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The roles of gut microbiota and susceptibility genes in patients with major depression disorder (MDD) are not well understood." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The contribution of different components to the AUC was evaluated by removing genetic information, microbiota abundance, and pathway data." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The gut microbiome was an important predictor of the response after eight weeks, while genetics was an important predictor of the response after two weeks." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "These results suggested a dynamic effect of interaction among genetics and gut microbes on treatment." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, these results provide new guidance for clinical decisions: in cases of inadequate treatment effects after two weeks, the composition of the intestinal flora can be improved by diet therapy, which could ultimately affect the efficacy." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Examining the microbiome and host genetics might be helpful for clinical decision-making." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Patients with MDD were recruited in this study and subsequently treated for eight weeks." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We identified the differences between the population with a response after two weeks and those with a response after eight weeks." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The factors that were significantly correlated with efficacy were used to predict the treatment response." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The differences in the importance of microbiota and genetics in prediction were analyzed." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our study identified rs58010457 as a potentially key locus affecting the treatment effect." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Different microbiota and enriched pathways might play different roles in the response after two and eight weeks." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37023596_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37023596> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that the area under the curve (AUC) value was greater than 0.8 for both random forest models." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37023596_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dysbiosis of the Gut Microbiota and Kynurenine (Kyn) Pathway Activity as Potential Biomarkers in Patients with Major Depressive Disorder." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "With increasing attention paid to the concept of the microbiota-gut-brain axis, mounting evidence reveals that the gut microbiota is involved in a variety of neurological and psychiatric diseases." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "These may result in increased neurotoxic metabolites and reduced generation of serotonin in the disease process." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "These changed factors may potentially be utilized as biomarkers for MDD in the future, playing more important roles in the disease course." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, gut microbiota changes in major depressive disorder (MDD) patients and their association with disease mechanisms remain undefined." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fifty MDD patients and sixty healthy controls were recruited from the Shanghai Healthy Mental Center, China." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal samples were collected, and the compositional characteristics of the intestinal flora were determined in MDD patients by MiSeq sequencing." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Venous blood was collected for the detection of plasma indoleamine-2,3-dioxygenase (Ido), kynurenine (Kyn) and tryptophan (Trp) levels." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Stool samples of bacterial 16S sequencing was carried out." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A total of 2,705,809 optimized sequences were obtained, with an average of 54,116 per sample." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "More unique OTUs were observed at the family, genus and species levels in the control group compared with the MDD cases." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37049591_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37049591> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Further analysis showed significant changes in the α- and β-diversities and relative abundance levels of gut microbial entities in MDD patients, as well as elevated amounts of Ido and Kyn indicating Kyn pathway activation, KEGG bacterial 16S function prediction analysis shows a variety of amino acids and metabolic (including Ido, Trp and Kyn) changes in the body of patients with MDD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37049591_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Development of the gut microbiota in the first 14 years of life and its relations to internalizing and externalizing difficulties and social anxiety during puberty." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Relations between the gut microbiota and host mental health have been suggested by a growing number of case-control and cross-sectional studies, while supporting evidence is limited in large community samples followed during an extended period." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The findings of this study continue to map gut microbiota development in a relatively large community sample followed from birth onwards, importantly extending our knowledge to puberty." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Results indicate that Prevotella 9 and Faecalibacterium may be relevant microbial taxa in relation to externalizing behavior and social anxiety, respectively." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "These correlational findings need validations from other similar cohort studies, as well as well-designed mechanistic pre-clinical investigations before inferring cause and effect." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, the current preregistered study ( https://osf.io/8ymav , September 7, 2022) described child gut microbiota development in the first 14 years of life and explored its relations to internalizing and externalizing difficulties and social anxiety in puberty, a period of high relevance for the development of mental health problems." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal microbiota composition was analysed by 16S ribosomal RNA gene amplicon sequencing in a total of 1003 samples from 193 children." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Through a clustering method, four distinct microbial clusters were newly identified in puberty." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most children within three of these clusters remained in the same clusters from the age of 12 to 14 years, suggesting stability in microbial development and transition during this period." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "These three clusters were compositionally similar to enterotypes (i.e., a robust classification of the gut microbiota based on its composition across different populations) enriched in Bacteroides, Prevotella, and Ruminococcus, respectively." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Two Prevotella 9-predominated clusters, including one reported by us earlier in middle childhood and the other one in puberty, were associated with more externalizing behavior at age 14." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "One Faecalibacterium-depleted pubertal cluster was related to more social anxiety at age 14." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37071196_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37071196> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This finding was confirmed by a negative cross-sectional relation between Faecalibacterium and social anxiety in the 14-year-olds." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37071196_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Positive mood-related gut microbiota in a long-term closed environment: a multiomics study based on the \"Lunar Palace 365\" experiment." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Psychological health risk is one of the most severe and complex risks in manned deep-space exploration and long-term closed environments." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "These observations reveal that gut microbiota contributed to a robust effect on the maintenance and improvement of mental health in a long-term closed environment." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our findings represent a key step towards a better understanding the role of the gut microbiome in mammalian mental health during space flight and provide a basis for future efforts to develop microbiota-based countermeasures that mitigate risks to crew mental health during future long-term human space expeditions on the moon or Mars." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study also provides an essential reference for future applications of psychobiotics to neuropsychiatric treatments." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Video Abstract." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recently, with the in-depth research of the microbiota-gut-brain axis, gut microbiota has been considered a new approach to maintain and improve psychological health." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, the correlation between gut microbiota and psychological changes inside long-term closed environments is still poorly understood." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Herein, we used the \"Lunar Palace 365\" mission, a 1-year-long isolation study in the Lunar Palace 1 (a closed manned Bioregenerative Life Support System facility with excellent performance), to investigate the correlation between gut microbiota and psychological changes, in order to find some new potential psychobiotics to maintain and improve the psychological health of crew members." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We report some altered gut microbiota that were associated with psychological changes in the long-term closed environment." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Four potential psychobiotics (Bacteroides uniformis, Roseburia inulinivorans, Eubacterium rectale, and Faecalibacterium prausnitzii) were identified." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "On the basis of metagenomic, metaproteomic, and metabolomic analyses, the four potential psychobiotics improved mood mainly through three pathways related to nervous system functions: first, by fermenting dietary fibers, they may produce short-chain fatty acids, such as butyric and propionic acids; second, they may regulate amino acid metabolism pathways of aspartic acid, glutamic acid, tryptophan, etc." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "(e.g., converting glutamic acid to gamma-aminobutyric acid; converting tryptophan to serotonin, kynurenic acid, or tryptamine); and third, they may regulate other pathways, such as taurine and cortisol metabolism." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37095530_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37095530> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, the results of animal experiments confirmed the positive regulatory effect and mechanism of these potential psychobiotics on mood." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37095530_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A systematic review on gut-brain axis aberrations in bipolar disorder and methods of balancing the gut microbiota." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bipolar disorder (BD) is a mood disorder that affects millions worldwide." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Probiotic supplementation was found to lower patient rehospitalizations and significantly improve depressive symptoms and cognitive impairments among patients with BD." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Multiple studies included in this review point toward a possible link between BD and the gut microbiota." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Probiotic supplements and other gut-balancing therapies could serve as effective adjunctive methods for the treatment of BD." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Notable limitations of the studies included for analysis were small sample sizes and majority observational study designs." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_14
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_14> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Furthermore, the microbiota aberrations found in patients with BD were not consistent across multiple studies." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_14" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_15
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_15> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Despite these limitations, our findings demonstrate the need for further research regarding the relationship between aberrant gut microbiota profiles and BD, as well as the effectiveness of gut balancing methods as adjunctive treatments." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_15" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Up to half of the diagnosed patients are reported to not receive adequate treatment." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This study aims to assess the relationship between the gut-brain axis and BD and to discuss and compare the efficacy of varying methods of balancing gut microbiotas in BD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Using PubMed, Embase, and Google Scholar from November 2021 to February 2022, we found 5310 studies on gut microbiota and its relation to BD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Using our inclusion criteria, 5283 studies were excluded." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A total of 27 full-text articles were assessed for eligibility." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Also, 12 articles that met our criteria and eligibility criteria reported on 613 BD patients." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most studies analyzed found an overall difference in gut microbiota composition in bipolar patients compared to healthy controls, though the alterations found were not consistent." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37127945_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37127945> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Differences in Lactobacillus, Faecalibacterium, and Ruminococcus abundance in BD compared to controls were found to be the most consistent across a few of the studies, but their effects on the gut-brain axis conflicted." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37127945_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Comparison of gut microbiome profile in patients with schizophrenia and healthy controls - A plausible non-invasive biomarker?" ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The human gut microbiome regulates brain function through the microbiome-gut-brain axis and is implicated in several neuropsychiatric disorders." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our findings contribute to a better understanding of the role of the gut microbiome in SCZ pathophysiology and suggest potential targeted interventions." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, the relationship between the gut microbiome and the pathogenesis of schizophrenia (SCZ) is poorly defined, and very few studies have examined the effect of antipsychotic treatment response." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We aim to study the differences in the gut microbiota among drug-naïve (DN SCZ) and risperidone-treated SCZ patients (RISP SCZ), compared to healthy controls (HCs)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We recruited a total of 60 participants, from the clinical services of a large neuropsychiatric hospital, which included DN SCZ, RISP SCZ and HCs (n = 20 each)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Fecal samples were analyzed using 16s rRNA sequencing in this cross-sectional study." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "No significant differences were found in taxa richness (alpha diversity) but microbial composition differed between SCZ patients (both DN and RISP) and HCs (PERMANOVA, p = 0.02)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Linear Discriminant Analysis Effect Size (LEfSe) and Random Forest model identified the top six genera, which significantly differed in abundance between the study groups." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A specific genus-level microbial panel of Ruminococcus, UCG005, Clostridium_sensu_stricto_1 and Bifidobacterium could discriminate SCZ patients from HCs with an area under the curve (AUC) of 0.79, HCs vs DN SCZ (AUC: 0.68), HCs vs RISP SCZ (AUC: 0.93) and DN SCZ vs RISP SCZ (AUC: 0.87)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37156128_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37156128> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Our study identified distinct microbial signatures that could aid in the differentiation of DN SCZ, RISP SCZ, and HCs." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37156128_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Features of gut microbiota and short-chain fatty acids in patients with first-episode depression and their relationship with the clinical symptoms." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "To compare the differences in gut microbiota and short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs; metabolites of gut microbiota) in the serum of patients with first-episode depression and the healthy population and to analyze the relationship between gut microbiota and metabolite SCFAs and the clinical symptoms of major depressive disorder (MDD)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A total of 45 patients with first-episode depression and 22 healthy volunteers were chosen to complete relevant scale evaluations, and feces samples and venous blood samples were collected." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The 16S RNA method was used to analyze the intestinal microflora and the characteristics of serum SCFAs detection by ELISA kit, as well as the intestinal flora, SCFAs content and their correlation with MDD clinical indicators." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The abundance of <i>Akkermansia</i>, <i>Megamonas</i>, <i>Prevotellaceae NK3B31 group</i>, and butyrate-producing bacteria, <i>Lachnospira</i>, <i>Subdoligranulum</i>, <i>Blautia</i>, and <i>Dialister</i>, and acetate-producing bacteria, <i>Streptococcus</i>, in the gut microbiota of the MDD group was lower than that in the control (C) group." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The abundance of <i>Parasutterella</i> in the MDD group was higher than that in the C group." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "<i>Dialister</i> negatively correlated with all measured clinical symptoms (<i>r</i> < 0, <i>P</i> < 0.05)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The serum SCFA content in the MDD group was higher than that in the C group, and the content positively correlated with the Hamilton anxiety scale scores (<i>r</i> = 0.584, <i>P</i> < 0.05)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37168424_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37168424> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The results demonstrated that the MDD group differed from the C group in terms of gut microbiota and SCFAs in the serum and that the change in certain intestinal bacteria might participate in the pathogenic mechanism of MDD." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37168424_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Anxiety Disorders and Gut Dysbiosis in Primary Sjögren's Syndrome-Mediated Dry Eye Patients." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Primary Sjögren's syndrome (pSS), a disease that is associated with a high prevalence of psychological disorders, has become increasingly important." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Prevotella was associated with dry eye severity (<i>p</i> <0.001)." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bacteroidetes (<i>p</i> =0.046) and Odoribacter (<i>p</i> =0.001) were correlated with pSS activity." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "There is a bidirectional relationship between anxiety disorder and the gut microbiota in pSS-mediated dry eye." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Alterations in certain classes of gut microbiota are associated with pSS activity and dry eye severity." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_14
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_14> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Main gut microbiota alterations that have a facilitating impact on anxiety are emerging in pSS-mediated dry eye." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_14" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_15
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_15> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Future studies are needed to explore specific therapeutic targets for improving mental health in pSS-mediated dry eye by microbiota intervention." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_15" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Interactions between the gut microbiota and ocular conditions have been identified in pSS." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "As mental intervention is frequently needed, this study aims to investigate the relationship between anxiety disorders and the gut microbiome in patients with pSS-mediated dry eye." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Demographics and self-administered questionnaires were obtained." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Faecal samples were evaluated using 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequencing." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS-A) cut-off point of ≥ 8 points showed a sensitivity and specificity of 76.5% and 80.0%, respectively." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In all participants, we found that the prevalence of anxiety disorder was 30.4%." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Dry eye discomfort could promote an anxious state, and conversely, anxiety could threaten tear film and increase the risk of pSS activity." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37193253_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37193253> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "There was a certain correlation between anxiety disorder and gut dysbiosis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37193253_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "How Toll-like receptors influence Parkinson's disease in the microbiome-gut-brain axis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recently, a large number of experimenters have found that the pathogenesis of Parkinson's disease may be related to the gut microbiome and proposed the microbiome-gut-brain axis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Studies have shown that Toll-like receptors, especially Toll-like receptor 2 (TLR2) and Toll-like receptor 4 (TLR4), are key mediators of gut homeostasis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition to their established role in innate immunity throughout the body, research is increasingly showing that the Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 signaling pathways shape the development and function of the gut and enteric nervous system." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Notably, Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 are dysregulated in Parkinson's disease patients and may therefore be identified as the core of early gut dysfunction in Parkinson's disease." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "To better understand the contribution of Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 dysfunction in the gut to early α-synuclein aggregation, we discussed the structural function of Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 and signal transduction of Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 in Parkinson's disease by reviewing clinical, animal models, and <i>in vitro</i> studies." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37207228_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37207228> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We also present a conceptual model of the pathogenesis of Parkinson's disease, in which microbial dysbiosis alters the gut barrier as well as the Toll-like receptor 2 and Toll-like receptor 4 signaling pathways, ultimately leading to a positive feedback loop for chronic gut dysfunction, promoting α-synuclein aggregation in the gut and vagus nerve." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37207228_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bacillus licheniformis prevents and reduces anxiety-like and depression-like behaviours." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "As common mental disorders, depression and anxiety impact people all around the world." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "KEY POINTS: • B. licheniformis reduced depressive-like and anxiety-like behaviours induced by the chronic unpredictable mild stress." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "• GABA levels in the brain are assonated with B. licheniformis regulating depressive-like and anxiety-like behaviours." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "• Gut microbiota composition alteration followed by metabolic changes may play a role in the GABA levels increase." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recent studies have found that the gut microbiome plays an important role in mental health." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "It is becoming possible to treat mental disorders by regulating the composition of the gut microbiota." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Bacillus licheniformis is a probiotic used to treat gut diseases through balancing the gut microbiome during lasting years." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Considering the role of gut microbiota in the gut-brain axis, this study used chronic unpredictable mild stress (CUMS) model rats to explore whether Bacillus licheniformis can prevent and treat depression and anxiety." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We found that B. licheniformis reduced the depressive-like and anxiety-like behaviours of the rats during the CUMS process." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Meanwhile, B. licheniformis changed the gut microbiota composition; increased the short chain fatty acids (SCFAs) in the colon, decreased kynurenine, norepinephrine, and glutamate levels; and increased the tryptophan, dopamine, epinephrine, and γ-aminobutyric acid (GABA) in the brain." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "After correlation analysis, we found Parabacteroides, Anaerostipes, Ruminococcus-2, and Blautia showed significant correlation with neurotransmitters and SCFAs, indicating the gut microbiome plays an important role in B. licheniformis reducing depressive-like behaviours." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37209162_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37209162> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, this study suggested B. licheniformis may prevent depressive-like and anxiety-like behaviours while regulating the gut microbiota composition and increasing the SCFA levels in the colon to alter the levels of the neurotransmitters in the brain." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37209162_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "IgA-Biome Profiles Correlate with Clinical Parkinson's Disease Subtypes." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Parkinson's disease is a heterogeneous neurodegenerative disorder with distinctive gut microbiome patterns suggesting that interventions targeting the gut microbiota may prevent, slow, or reverse disease progression and severity." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Because secretory IgA (SIgA) plays a key role in shaping the gut microbiota, characterization of the IgA-Biome of individuals classified into either the akinetic rigid (AR) or tremor dominant (TD) Parkinson's disease clinical subtypes was used to further define taxa unique to these distinct clinical phenotypes." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Flow cytometry was used to separate IgA-coated and -uncoated bacteria from stool samples obtained from AR and TD patients followed by amplification and sequencing of the V4 region of the 16 S rDNA gene on the MiSeq platform (Illumina)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "IgA-Biome analyses identified significant alpha and beta diversity differences between the Parkinson's disease phenotypes and the Firmicutes/Bacteroides ratio was significantly higher in those with TD compared to those with AR." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition, discriminant taxa analyses identified a more pro-inflammatory bacterial profile in the IgA+ fraction of those with the AR clinical subclass compared to IgA-Biome analyses of those with the TD subclass and with the taxa identified in the unsorted control samples." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "IgA-Biome analyses underscores the importance of the host immune response in shaping the gut microbiome potentially affecting disease progression and presentation." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37212075_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37212075> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the present study, IgA-Biome analyses identified a unique proinflammatory microbial signature in the IgA+ fraction of those with AR that would have otherwise been undetected using conventional microbiome analysis approaches." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37212075_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Global research trends and focus on the link between colorectal cancer and gut flora: a bibliometric analysis from 2001 to 2021." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Colorectal cancer (CRC) is a highly prevalent cancer, and the global healthcare system bears a significant burden due to its incidence." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The United States and China are the main contributors in this field and have established a network of partnerships in several countries." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "414 academic journals have published articles on this topic." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The author with the highest number of publications is Jun Yu from the Chinese University of Hong Kong." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "In addition to \"intestinal flora\" and \"colorectal cancer,\" high frequency terms in the keyword co-occurrence network analysis included inflammatory bowel disease, <i>Fusobacterium nucleatum</i>, inflammation, long-chain fatty acids, ulcerative colitis, bile acids, and resistant starch." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_14
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_14> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Analysis of keyword trends using burst testing revealed that biomarkers, abnormal crypt foci, bifidobacteria, β-glucuronidase, short-chain fatty acids, bile acids, and DNA methylation are at the forefront of research in this area." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_14" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_15
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_15> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The findings of this study provide a bibliometric analysis and visualization of the key research areas in gut microbiota and CRC over the past 20 years." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_15" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_16
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_16> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The results suggest that the role of gut microbiota in CRC and its underlying mechanisms should be closely monitored, particularly in the areas of biomarkers, metabolic pathways, and DNA methylation, which may emerge as hot topics in this field." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_16" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Modulating the gut microbiota is a promising approach to enhance the efficacy of CRC treatment and reduce its adverse effects." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The causal relationship between specific microorganisms' presence and CRC development has been widely validated." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "However, few studies have investigated this relationship using bibliometric methods." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Therefore, this study analyzed the research hotspots and trends in human gut microbiology and CRC over the last two decades from a bibliometric perspective." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The study aims to provide novel insights into basic and clinical research in this field." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The articles and reviews on gut microbiota in CRC were obtained from the Web of Science Core Collection (WOSCC) on November 2, 2022." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "CiteSpace and VOSviewer were used to conduct the bibliometric and knowledge-map analysis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37213508_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37213508> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A total of 2,707 publications were obtained, with a rapid increase in the number of publications since 2015." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37213508_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The microbiota-gut-brain axis and three common neurological disorders: a mini-review." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Neurological disorders are an important cause of disability and death globally." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_10
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_10> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The number of gut microbiota is much more than the number of body cells." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_10" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_11
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_11> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "Gut microbiota has been regarded as a crucial regulator of the gut-brain axis." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_11" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_12
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_12> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "The discovery of the microbiota-gut-brain axis is described as a major advancement in neuroscience because it influences the pathophysiology of several neurological and psychiatric disorders." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_12" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_13
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_13> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                       gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                              gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                              gutprop:hasSentenceText "From this, more studies of the microbiota-gut-brain axis are needed in the future, to provide a better understanding of brain disorders and so that better treatment and prognosis." ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_13" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Recently, a large body of research shows that the gut microbiome affects the brain and its conditions, through the gut-brain axis." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The purpose of this mini-review is to provide a brief overview of the relationship between the microbiota-gut-brain axis in three neurological disorders: epilepsy, Parkinson's disease, and migraine." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The authors chose these three disorders because of their burdensome and great effect on health care." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "We live on a microbial planet." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Before humans, microorganisms existed for a hundred million years." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Today, there are trillions of these microbes living in our bodies, it is called human microbiota." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_7" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_8
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_8> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "These organisms have a crucial role in our homeostasis and survival." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_8" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_9
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37228957_9> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37228957> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Most of the human microbiota live in the gut." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37228957_9" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_0
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_0> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/title/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "A comprehensive look at the psychoneuroimmunoendocrinology of spinal cord injury and its progression: mechanisms and clinical opportunities." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_0" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_1
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_1> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Spinal cord injury (SCI) is a devastating and disabling medical condition generally caused by a traumatic event (primary injury)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_1" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_2
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_2> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "This initial trauma is accompanied by a set of biological mechanisms directed to ameliorate neural damage but also exacerbate initial damage (secondary injury)." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_2" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_3
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_3> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The alterations that occur in the spinal cord have not only local but also systemic consequences and virtually all organs and tissues of the body incur important changes after SCI, explaining the progression and detrimental consequences related to this condition." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_3" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_4
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_4> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Psychoneuroimmunoendocrinology (PNIE) is a growing area of research aiming to integrate and explore the interactions among the different systems that compose the human organism, considering the mind and the body as a whole." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_4" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_5
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_5> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "The initial traumatic event and the consequent neurological disruption trigger immune, endocrine, and multisystem dysfunction, which in turn affect the patient's psyche and well-being." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_5" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_6
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_6> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "In the present review, we will explore the most important local and systemic consequences of SCI from a PNIE perspective, defining the changes occurring in each system and how all these mechanisms are interconnected." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_6" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_7
<https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/sentence/37291666_7> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                                                      gutprop:Sentence ;
                                                                             gutprop:partOf <https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/abstract/37291666> ;
                                                                             gutprop:hasSentenceText "Finally, potential clinical approaches derived from this knowledge will also be collectively presented with the aim to develop integrative therapies to maximize the clinical management of these patients." ;
                                                                             rdfs:label "sentence_37291666_7" .


