                                                                                                      rdfs:comment "The Bray-Curtis dissimilarity is a measure of dissimilarity between two samples in ecology and microbiology, calculated as half the absolute difference between the two samples' abundance profiles. [Definition Source: llama3-8b-8192]" ;
                                                                                                      rdfs:label "Bray Curtis Dissimilarity" .


###  https://w3id.org/hereditary/ontology/gutbrain/resource/statisticaltechnique/Chao1Index
