                                                                                                                dcterms:creator "Samuel Piron" ;
                                                                                                                rdfs:comment "Inverse Variance Weighted (IVW) MR analysis is a Mendelian Randomization method that combines the causal effect estimates from multiple genetic variants, weighting each by the inverse of its variance, to produce an overall estimate of the exposure’s effect on an outcome. [Definition Source: OpenAi 4o]" ;
                                                                                                                rdfs:label "Inverse Variance Weighted Mr Analysis" .


